<Bindings>
    <!--
      The keybinding docs/FLOW.md has described since it was written.

      That document lays out the nightly path as "/warband, Enter, Ctrl+C, or
      keybind bar button" and calls it the sub-two-second loop repeated four to
      ten times an evening. No BINDING_* was ever registered, so the real path
      was five actions — Enter, type the command, Enter, Ctrl+C, Esc — two of
      them chat-line typing, which a stuck chat focus eats.

      One binding, on the toggle rather than on a tab: the window opens on the
      export panel and that is what the key is for. Combat is handled where the
      toggle already handles it — the request queues and fires on
      PLAYER_REGEN_ENABLED — so this needs no protection of its own.

      It is deliberately unbound by default. A binding this addon assigned for
      itself would take a key the player has already given to something else.
    -->
    <Binding name="WARBANDPRO_TOGGLE" header="WARBANDPRO" category="WarbandPro">
        WarbandPro_ToggleFromBinding()
    </Binding>
</Bindings>
